WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Let's make A snowy pinecone forest.

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:07.457
Stand pinecones in reusable clay, dab a little white paint onto the scales and

3
00:00:07.457 --> 00:00:09.765
arrange them into a tiny winter forest.

4
00:00:10.145 --> 00:00:12.225
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:12.605 --> 00:00:15.335
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.960
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.405
An adult checks cone scales and the paint label.

8
00:00:21.785 --> 00:00:24.290
Protect the table and wash hands afterward.

9
00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:28.155
Painted cones must not be returned to natural habitats.

10
00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:30.857
Step 1.

11
00:00:31.237 --> 00:00:33.082
Prepare three tree bases.

12
00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:36.907
Flatten each piece of clay into a small disc on the tray.

13
00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:41.512
Space the three discs apart, leaving a clear path between them.

14
00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:43.957
Keep unused paint closed.

15
00:00:44.337 --> 00:00:45.717
Grown-up help.

16
00:00:46.097 --> 00:00:48.902
Check the cones and protect the workspace.

17
00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:51.514
Step 2.

18
00:00:51.894 --> 00:00:53.754
Stand the pinecone trees.

19
00:00:54.134 --> 00:00:56.869
Press the wide end of each cone into a clay disc.

20
00:00:57.249 --> 00:00:59.254
Keep the cones upright and low.

21
00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:03.729
If one leans, widen its clay base and press it in a little more.

22
00:01:04.109 --> 00:01:05.489
Grown-up help.

23
00:01:05.869 --> 00:01:09.129
Help press pointed or awkward cones safely.

24
00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.012
Step 3.

25
00:01:12.392 --> 00:01:14.047
Make a light snow dab.

26
00:01:14.427 --> 00:01:17.407
Put one teaspoon of paint on a scrap of card.

27
00:01:17.787 --> 00:01:21.654
Touch the sponge to the paint, then dab once on the scrap so it

28
00:01:21.654 --> 00:01:22.482
is not dripping.

29
00:01:22.862 --> 00:01:24.242
Grown-up help.

30
00:01:24.622 --> 00:01:28.102
Read the paint label and help prepare the small amount.

31
00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:30.651
Step 4.

32
00:01:31.031 --> 00:01:32.256
Add snowy tips.

33
00:01:32.636 --> 00:01:36.486
Dab a little white paint on the outer tips of the cone scales.

34
00:01:36.866 --> 00:01:40.586
Leave brown spaces between dabs so the cone still shows.

35
00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:43.731
Turn the tray rather than holding the wet cone.

36
00:01:44.111 --> 00:01:45.491
Grown-up help.

37
00:01:45.871 --> 00:01:49.706
Help reach awkward areas without touching sharp scales.

38
00:01:51.168 --> 00:01:52.343
Step 5.

39
00:01:52.723 --> 00:01:54.408
Let the forest dry.

40
00:01:54.788 --> 00:01:59.073
Leave the tray flat until the paint is dry, following its label.

41
00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:03.278
Trace an imaginary path between the trees and name the forest.

42
00:02:03.658 --> 00:02:06.158
Wash the sponge and everyone’s hands.

43
00:02:06.538 --> 00:02:07.918
Grown-up help.

44
00:02:08.298 --> 00:02:11.613
Manage paint cleanup and check drying before handling.

45
00:02:13.001 --> 00:02:15.916
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

46
00:02:16.296 --> 00:02:19.846
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

47
00:02:20.226 --> 00:02:22.246
Your creation can look different.

48
00:02:22.626 --> 00:02:24.816
Remove clay for reuse where clean.

49
00:02:25.196 --> 00:02:30.745
Dispose of painted cones as craft waste according to local rules; never return them

50
00:02:30.745 --> 00:02:31.141
outdoors.

51
00:02:31.521 --> 00:02:33.296
Keep indoors and dry.

52
00:02:33.676 --> 00:02:37.196
Paint drying time depends on the product and amount used.

53
00:02:37.576 --> 00:02:38.566
Well done.

54
00:02:38.946 --> 00:02:41.376
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

